@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Hello, world!</h1>

<img src="thumbs-up.gif" alt="Thumbs Up" style="width: 200px; height: auto;" />
<p>Welcome to your new app.</p>
<li>
    This is our spreadsheet application. It has a very typical user interface, with a grid of cells that can be selected via a mouse click.
    During the selection of a cell a textbox above will be focused, and you can edit the contents of the cell. 
</li>
<li>
    The application also has the menu bar at the side where you can access our spreadsheet application.
</li>
<li>
    We display the value of a cell in the cell grid itself, during the editing process the textbox will display the contents of the cell,
    and when you are done editing the cell, the value will be displayed in the cell grid.
</li>
<li>
    The application interfacing with the razor component is done via the Spreadsheet class, and the view is updated via the
    following class properties: FileSaveName, CellsBackingStore, SelectedRow, SelectedCol, FocusedTextInput. and SelectedCellName.
</li>
<li>
    We are using property bindings to update the view when properties change. We choose this over using events because it 
    allows us to have a more declarative approach when the user interacts with the application, and at the same time it
    allows for a reactive state within the webpage aswell.
</li>

<h2>Additional Feature: Dark Mode</h2>
<p>
    We added a light/dark theme toggle to the spreadsheet. The button is in the toolbar next to Save and Load,
    and it switches between "🌙 Dark mode" and "☀ Light mode".
</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>How it works:</strong> The theme is stored as a <code>data-theme</code> attribute ("light" or "dark")
        on the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element. The CSS defines colors as variables (such as <code>--page-bg</code>
        and <code>--sheet-header-bg</code>) and overrides them under <code>html[data-theme="dark"]</code>. Switching
        themes only changes that one attribute, and the stylesheet does the rest. This covers the page, the top row,
        the table (via Bootstrap's <code>--bs-table-*</code> variables), and text inputs.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Persistence:</strong> The chosen theme is saved in the browser's <code>localStorage</code>. On first
        visit, the app follows the operating system's <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> setting.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>AI assistance:</strong> An AI assistant helped write the theme script, the dark-mode CSS and the
        toggle button. It was used only for this additional feature, as the assignment allows.
    </li>
</ul>